# The rollback backup is a verbatim copy of every row BEFORE fictionalisation:
# the real person's name, their three real employers, their home town, their
# phone number and the whole coaching transcript. Committing it would put the
# identity this exercise exists to remove into git history permanently, where
# deleting the file later would not take it back out.
#
# It is written locally on every run of 01-rename.js, which is where it is
# useful and the only place it should ever live.
output/rename-backup.json

# The placeholder rollback. Clean of any real identity (those rows were already
# fictionalised before they were deleted), but it is a local rollback artifact
# rather than source, and the same rule applies: backups stay on the machine
# that made them.
output/removed-placeholders.json
